<title>BOTSWANA: FNB Botswana year share rises, div up.</title>
<headline>FNB Botswana year share rises, div up.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Sept 30 1996</p>
<p>		    (million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Share (thebe)		  460   vs  405</p>
<p>    Dividend (thebe)		28   vs  24</p>
<p>    Net income		   77.27   vs  64.73</p>
<p>    Net interest income	53.95   vs  45.87</p>
<p>    Other operating income   27.39   vs  19.21</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge  4.06   vs   0.35</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			29.56   vs  24,52</p>
<p>    Tax			     7.18   vs   5.23</p>
<p>Full name: First National Bank of Botswana Limited</p>
<p>Div payable: Dec 13</p>
<p>On register: Nov 22</p>
<p>NOTE - The bank said the almost 12-fold increase in its bad debt charge was a result of the slowdown Botswana's economy coupled with the bank's rapid expansion.</p>
<p>Directors were confident with the continued active sourcing of new business and tighter controls on costs, the bank would sustain steady future growth.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom, +267 347-182</p>
</text>
